  "id": "statistical-control",
  "term": "statistical control",
  "definition": "Statistical control is the use of calculated control limits from statistical measures to judge whether observed data stay within an expected normal range or indicate a meaningful deviation. In this context, it separates normal conditions from failure or other abnormal change in a monitored process.",
